# --- The archive data -------------------------------------------------------
# gww_all.nc is ~503 MB and the chunk set ~900 MB. Git cannot carry them:
# GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MB, and Git LFS's free tier is only
# 1 GB of storage and 1 GB of bandwidth a month, which one clone would exhaust.
# The NetCDF is published as a GitHub release asset (2 GB limit) and on Zenodo,
# which is what the DOI in README.md points at.
data/
*.nc
*.nc.tmp

# --- Tooling ----------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is the published archive: documentation and the worked
# example. The downloader that produced the data is kept out deliberately --
# the download is a one-off (one more refresh planned for late 2026), so it is
# not part of the deliverable. Remove these lines to publish it too.
download_gww.py
DEVELOPMENT.md
SKILL.md
requirements.txt

# --- Working files ----------------------------------------------------------
download.log
*.log
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Output written by example_timeseries.ipynb when a reader runs it.
reservoir_*.csv
reservoir_*.png
